(Bug #74: the type lock could not see through a `'s <property>` read. Every
 property but `first`/`last` answered "type unknown", so #65's declaration
 check stayed silent, codegen stored the list's length in the text's slot,
 and Print dereferenced 3 as a pointer: segfault. LANGUAGE.md's List
 Properties table types `length` Number, and LANGUAGE.md:531-532 fixes a
 variable's type at its declaration - this is that sentence, read through a
 property.)

a list called counts is [10, 20, 30].
a text called tally is counts's length.
Print tally.
